Stage 2 research status (2026-11-03): Python implemented and executed a restricted, indivisible-token posted-price search subeconomy with newly produced services. Nine Stage 2 tests passed locally, alongside six original Stage 0 Aiyagari checks.

No-trade proposition: strictly increasing own-asset value and a pure zero-sum asset transfer imply only delta=0 satisfies both bilateral participation constraints.

Optimal active search candidate: M=5, mean=2, beta=.96, buyer utility=5, seller effort cost=.15; all participation gains nonnegative and Bellman/mass/market identities hold. A no-trade equilibrium also exists.

Boltzmann gain-loss operator follows exactly from matched buyer/seller events. Its weak form preserves mass and token holdings, while the service production rate is separately counted. Monte Carlo convergence was checked for 1500/6000/20000 agents and four seeds.

Uniform matching yields a truncated-geometric money stationary distribution and coincident mean-constrained max-entropy money distribution; assortative matching violates this coincidence (KL=.0060626683). A stylized Foley-style transaction entropy comparison gives KL=.19240049/.35979716, but differs in offer sets and is NOT a refutation of Foley.

Theoretical boundary: the productive Aiyagari block can coexist under strong separability, but nonseparable optimizing joint capital/money decisions, price bargaining, a shared labor constraint and monetary equilibrium selection are not solved. Maintain a restricted/partial status in plan.json and paper/article.qmd. Next priority: Lagos-Wright canonical mechanism and full joint household Bellman with endogenous exchange terms.

Product check executed: separable Aiyagari-money joint invariant measure sup error 2.45e-13, additive policy Bellman sup error 9.22e-12, goods/capital/token/service clearing verified. This requires independent sectors and cannot support claims of nonseparable GE integration.
